      "exampleEnglish": "I work in an office.",
      "grammarNote": "عمل conjugates exactly like ذهب and شرب — fully regular, following the same أَ-/تَ-/تَ...ينَ/يَ-/نَ- prefix template you've now drilled repeatedly. Its past tense (not tested separately in this level) follows the same suffix pattern too: عَمِلْتُ (I/you/you/she worked, the same collision-group as always), عَمِلَ (he worked), عَمِلْنَا (we worked) — you already have all the tools to recognize it.",
